  "trust_boundary": "Shared-host trust boundary: the worker, the actor transcript, and the SQLite sink share one OS user. File permissions do not separate them. The harness owns writes. A commit is inserted only through EffectSink after the harness write token matches the hash stored in harness_ownership. The actor transcript writer and the read-only observer do not hold that token. The observer opens the database with mode=ro and reads committed rows. A same-uid process that bypasses the API and writes SQL directly is outside this boundary. This experiment does not claim OS isolation. A passing local control or URL allowlist does not establish the broader system property.",
